# {{lb|hu|after an interrogative word}} [[again]] {{gloss|used in a question to ask something one has forgotten}}
#: {{uxi|hu|Hogy '''is''' hívják?|What's that called, '''again'''?}}
# [[sure enough]], [[indeed]]
#: {{syn|hu|tényleg|valóban|csakugyan}}
#: {{uxi|hu|Aznapra esőt mondtak, és el '''is''' kezdett esni.|Rain had been predicted for that day and, '''sure enough''', it was beginning to rain.|lit=They had said rain for…}}

====Usage notes====
When it is used with a [[concessive]] adverb (“no matter what/​who​/​when/how”, “however [good, bad]”, “long as it was”, “even if…” etc.), it is traditionally placed after the verb, though it is common in colloquial style to use it after the adverb instead:
: {{ux|hu|''(traditionally, chiefly in literary style)'' Bármilyen hosszúra nyúlt '''is''' az előadás,…<br/>''(more recently)'' Bármilyen hosszúra '''is''' nyúlt az előadás,…|No matter how long the lecture​/​performance stretched,…}}
It applies to [[Appendix:Hungarian verb-final set phrases|verb-final set phrases]] as well, similarly to {{m|hu|érez|érzi magát}} in this clause: {{m|hu||még ha ettől rosszul érezzük '''is''' magunkat / …rosszul '''is''' érezzük magunkat|even if it makes us feel bad}}.<!-- in the original, of which it is not a literal translation: "no matter how queasy it 
makes us feel" -->

